# Nullable narrowing remains branch-local

Verifies a direct non-null guard enables arithmetic only in its true branch and
does not change the binding's effective type after the branch.

>>> source
let value: int? = 10
if (value != null) {
    print(value + 1)
}
print(value + 2)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: nullable value must be narrowed before this operation at Span { start: 71, end: 76 }

<<< exit
1
